---
const links = [
  ["hot : cold", "opposites"],
  ["kitten : cat", "young → adult"],
  ["carpenter : wood", "person → material"],
  ["foot : walk", "hand : hold, a body part and its action"]
];
---

<div class="topic-sheet">
  <h1>Cloze and Analogies - Fit and connect</h1>
  <section class="summary-block summary-peach">
    <h2>Cloze</h2>
    <p>A cloze blank needs the word that makes the sentence make sense. It tests meaning and grammar together.</p>
    <p>She was so <strong>generous</strong> that everyone liked her. Generous fits, because people liked her. Fierce, clumsy and angry do not match that idea.</p>
    <p>Read the sentence again with your word in place. It must sound natural and match the tone.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="summary-block summary-yellow">
    <h2>Analogies</h2>
    <p>An analogy is a link between one pair of words that you apply to a second pair.</p>
    <table class="punct-table summary-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="th-feature" scope="col">Pair</th>
          <th class="th-example" scope="col">Relationship</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          links.map(([pair, relationship]) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{pair}</th>
              <td>{relationship}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>“Pencil is to write as brush is to ___?” The answer is <strong>paint</strong>.</p>
    <p>Ask how the first two words are connected. Then use that same link for the second pair.</p>
  </section>
</div>
